{"evt":"note_created","id":"note-mqgvjghmn2z","workspace":"D:\\zonoid","title":"Headless judge and label drains deadlock the daemon: spawnSync blocks the event loop while the spawned child calls back over HTTP","summary":"CONFIRMED root cause (symptom: daemon froze and blocked all work after a 5-min drain tick). lib/headless-drain.js runDrain uses spawnSync, which blocks the daemon's single-threaded Node event loop for the entire child run. The JUDGE drain spawns a headless claude -p that must call GET /judge/next + POST /judge/verdict back on the SAME daemon, and the LABEL drain's gate-label.js also talks HTTP to it — but a daemon frozen in spawnSync cannot serve those callbacks, so the child hangs until the 10-min timeout and writes nothing. The LEARNER drain survives only because it writes a JSON file and does not call back to the daemon, which is exactly why the learner-first design passed review while judge/label silently fail in production. The 40 unit tests MOCK spawnSync, so none exercised a real child calling into a frozen daemon (unit-green, integration-broken). Secondary finding: the headless claude -p judge is a FULL Claude Code session — captured stdout shows it running SessionStart hooks; even with a free daemon it spent 75s in startup without reaching judging, so each run is minutes. THE FIX: convert runDrain (and runDueDrains) from spawnSync to async child_process.spawn so the daemon event loop stays free to serve the drains' HTTP callbacks; update the governor accounting + the daemon.js trigger to the async shape; replace the spawnSync mocks in test/headless-drain.test.js with an integration test that exercises a real callback. CURRENT STATE: feature is merged to main (8e9024a) but DISABLED — ORCH_HEADLESS_DRAINS set to 0 in .mcp.json and .claude/settings.json, daemon relaunched flag-off (PID 51368). Do NOT re-enable the flag until the async-spawn fix lands. DEPENDENCY (build into bin/install.js): turning headless judge drains on requires the Claude Code CLI installed AND authenticated (the runner spawns claude -p, resolved via lib/claude-cli.js); the installer must verify/wire this, plus stop clobbering .mcp.json env on reinstall and add a --headless-drains opt-in.","created_by":"main","valid_from":"2026-06-16T16:46:25.594Z","vec":[-0.09341952204704285,0.03782378509640694,-0.11611447483301163,-0.002691575326025486,0.040571752935647964,-0.05467025563120842,-0.011713742278516293,0.04210343211889267,0.004385506268590689,0.058644767850637436,0.002890377538278699,0.00939086265861988,-0.02706081047654152,-0.05565526708960533,-0.040274228900671005,-0.0063235280103981495,0.0614478774368763,-0.030610620975494385,-0.016180016100406647,-0.023462101817131042,0.00374893331900239,-0.03259173780679703,0.07318652421236038,0.017061976715922356,-0.07050720602273941,-0.06657629460096359,-0.12734746932983398,-0.07666322588920593,-0.01029106043279171,-0.07094331085681915,0.012285212986171246,-0.003622115356847644,-0.111543208360672,-0.0879857987165451,0.02013932727277279,0.08024929463863373,0.04564713314175606,-0.029064420610666275,-0.11487580835819244,0.013751257210969925,0.10146784782409668,0.08640133589506149,-0.0867723748087883,-0.01925235241651535,-0.026812100782990456,-0.012765138410031796,-0.06725534796714783,-0.06029988452792168,-0.03535545989871025,-0.028260743245482445,-0.00016700191190466285,-0.011472919024527073,0.057922594249248505,0.01714938133955002,-0.008538010530173779,0.009688163176178932,0.07031654566526413,0.06213441491127014,-0.012000901624560356,0.060004957020282745,-0.03653969243168831,0.0342932865023613,-0.03656386956572533,-0.0009618307813070714,0.05592573061585426,0.0171546321362257,0.008495029993355274,-0.04414611682295799,0.05323750525712967,-0.029748868197202682,-0.0020676094572991133,0.041376229375600815,-0.010150429792702198,-0.03339134901762009,-0.026061583310365677,0.038914453238248825,0.007338616997003555,0.02908024750649929,0.030928952619433403,-0.10965293645858765,-0.09676209092140198,-0.042511